          "text": "Rob Stump is running for At-large Town Council Member in the Town of Los Gatos. He has not called the killing in Gaza a genocide and has not backed any effort to block U.S. weapons transfers or economic aid to Israel. The Bay Area Muslim Council Action opposed Stump, but its stated reason was his record as a planning commissioner — a matter of local governance, not of Palestine policy. That distinction matters: the opposition does not rest on any contrary act or silence on the question of Israeli violence against Palestinians. Mary Badame, also on the ballot, drew opposition from the same group, but that call was tactical rather than grounded in any policy finding, and Badame herself has made no public statements or taken any actions on the Palestine question. Between two candidates neither of whom has taken a public stand on Palestine, Stump is the stronger choice because the documented reason for his opposition is a specific, bounded governance question rather than an unexplained tactical call, and nothing he has done reflects a refusal to stand with Palestinians when the moment called for it.",
